.SH BUGS
.B -t
drives the rules, the join, the pad, the state, the held descriptors and
the unmount.
It presses no key: the tables that turn a key into an action are covered
by nothing and have only ever been checked by playing.
.PP
Two people have never played it at once.
Everything below that \- two clients, two pads, two players moving \- is
checked, but by one process writing both pads.
.PP
There is no authentication and no attempt at one.
Anybody who can reach the port can write anybody's pad, including yours.
.PP
Nothing times out.
A client that stops reading does not stop the game, but a client reading
from a wedged server waits for ever.
.PP
The catch-up is bounded at eight frames a read, so a client that stops
reading for a second and comes back sees the game behind where the wall
clock says it should be, and it stays behind.
